BRAND ASSETS EXCEPTION

The MIT License above applies to the software in this repository. It does NOT
apply to the brand assets listed below, which are excluded from that grant:

  - vendor/henry-mascot/            (the henry-mascot submodule, in full; it
                                     carries its own all-rights-reserved LICENSE)
  - src/vendor/henry/               (Henry's working files, synced from the
                                     submodule by scripts/sync-henry.js)
  - public/favicon.ico
  - public/favicon-16x16.png
  - public/favicon-32x32.png
  - public/apple-touch-icon.png
  - public/android-chrome-192x192.png
  - public/android-chrome-512x512.png
  - public/404.html                 (generated from scripts/404.template.html
                                     with henry-animated.css inlined; the
                                     template itself is software under the MIT
                                     License, the generated page depicts Henry)
  - every build output derived from the above: the favicons at the site root,
    static/media/henry-illustration-*.svg, and the henry-animated.css rules
    inlined into each prerendered HTML file, in build/ and on the deployed
    site

The synced copies under src/vendor/henry/ and public/, including the
generated public/404.html, are gitignored and regenerated at install time, so they are absent from the tracked tree but
present in every working checkout and every build. They are excluded
wherever they appear.

These files depict "Henry," a robot mascot that is Copyright (c) Curt Henrichs,
all rights reserved. Henry is a brand mascot, not clip art.

You may fork this repository, deploy your own site, and use the software
freely under the MIT License. You may not use Henry as the identity of your
own project, whether or not your copy is derived from this one.

Removing or replacing these assets is expressly permitted, and is the intended
path for a fork: the software carries no dependency on them that a substitute
mark placed at the same paths cannot satisfy.
